# Bilingual Support (i18n)

## Languages

- English: `en`
- Mizo: `lus` (ISO 639-3)

## Implementation

- Use `react-i18next` with `expo-localization`
- Translation files in `/locales/{en,lus}/*.json`
- AI-first translation (Gemini) with human review for cultural terms
- All content supports dual-language entries

## Usage Pattern

```typescript
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';

const MyComponent = () => {
  const { t } = useTranslation();
  
  return <Text>{t('common.welcome')}</Text>;
};
```

## Translation File Structure

```
/locales/
  /en/
    common.json
    auth.json
    content.json
  /lus/
    common.json
    auth.json
    content.json
```

## Content Model

Database content entries support both languages:

```typescript
interface Content {
  title_en: string;
  title_lus: string;
  body_en: string;
  body_lus: string;
}
```
